# Mission plan

## Objectives

1. **Create** new documentation files with a user-approved name, location, and
   document shape — or **change** an existing file the user names — under a
   folder registered in **`.sedea/documentation-management.yaml`**.
2. Keep the working copy aligned with the remote via **`rclone bisync`** before
   and after edits (the user may change files outside Sedea agents).
3. Produce an approved plan (Background, Desired Outcomes, Proposed Changes,
   Unresolved Questions/Unknowns) with cited sources, then author the document
   from that plan.
4. Resolve bisync conflicts through the spawned **file-synchronizer** skill —
   structured choice when local and remote change intent diverges semantically.
5. When the folder has **`source-of-truth/`**, consult it while authoring; after
   the document is complete, **report** any deviations (where they occurred and
   suggested SoT-oriented fixes) in Mission Control / ops docs — **not** by
   naming SoT inside the authored file (center rule **20** § *Authored document
   output hygiene*). Do **not** write SoT in this mission — the user refreshes
   SoT via **`refresh source of truth`** (**source-of-truth-folder**) in a
   separate dispatch when they choose. Do **not** consult
   **`source-of-truth/CHANGELOG.md`** as authoritative SoT when authoring or
   when comparing deviations, unless the user **explicitly** refers to the
   change log and explains how to use it for that turn (rule **20** § *Change
   log (audit only)*). Ops deviation reports remain under
   **`operationsDocsDirectory`**; they are not the in-folder change log.
6. Close the dispatch with an explicit Squad Leader resolution proposal when the
   pass is complete, partially complete, or abandoned.
7. Optionally convert the authored source to PDF after outbound sync:
   documentation-folder destination with remote sync, operations-docs link only,
   or skip — without replacing the source document. Conversion mechanics live in
   the **Convert Document** mission; this mission only chooses the export mode
   and hands off.

