### Drive format pairing (local Office ↔ native Google Docs)

**Binding for §4, §7, and [skills/file-synchronizer/SKILL.md](skills/file-synchronizer/SKILL.md).**
PDF conversion (§8a) already uses import/export formats; source-document sync
must do the same.

**Problem:** Local working copies are often **`.docx`**. Remotes on Google Drive
are often **native Google Docs** (`application/vnd.google-apps.document`). Uploading
or bisyncing the local Office file as a binary `.docx` **fails** when the remote
name maps to a Google Doc — this is a **format-pair** failure, not (usually) missing
SA auth.

**Procedure (typed detection — not trial-and-error):**

1. **Local kind** — from `relativeFilePath` extension (for example `.docx`).
2. **Remote kind** — one **`rclone lsjson`** (or equivalent) on the remote object
   with the same SA / root-folder flags as **`10_required-tools.mdc`** § Drive auth.
   Read Drive **`MimeType`** / rclone mime fields. Treat
   **`application/vnd.google-apps.document`** as **native Google Doc**.
3. **Apply the flag table** (below). Do **not** loop random flag combinations.
4. If remote kind is **unknown** or probe fails after auth succeeds →
   USER_CHECKPOINT (ask whether the remote is a native Google Doc / Office file /
   other) — **forbidden:** blind retries or reconnect-first.

| Local | Remote | Inbound (§4 / pull) | Outbound (§7 / push / file-synchronizer sync) |
|-------|--------|---------------------|-----------------------------------------------|
| `.docx` | Native Google Doc | `--drive-export-formats docx` | `--drive-import-formats docx` |
| `.docx` | Office / binary `.docx` | (no import/export pair flags) | (no import/export pair flags) |
| Native export path / non-docx | Native Google Doc | Use matching `--drive-export-formats` when local expects that type | Do not invent Office import without a local Office file |

**Always** keep required auth flags from **`10_required-tools.mdc`**
(`--drive-service-account-file`, `--drive-root-folder-id` when applicable).

**Forbidden:** treating “upload refused” / cryptic Drive errors as opaque auth
failure before checking this table; suggesting **`rclone config reconnect`** for
format-pair failures; inventing a second sync engine.

**Follow-up (out of scope here):** per-document sync metadata (sidecar or registry
`files:` map) so agents can skip the remote probe — larger center schema change.

